;;; A query's `:goal` whose `(absent …)` writes a pattern inside a pattern with a
;;; variable as its relation loads, and holds in every state —
;;; M1f **W79**, register row `W79/goal-absent-nested-relation-variable`, filed by S1f.7.1 (T1f.7.1.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `goal-nested-relation-variable.ein` with its goal negated: `(absent (says (?R
;;; ?g)))`, nothing is said.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Refused at load, as the pattern is without the `(absent …)`, one line, on every
;;; command (exit 1, `ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `73a0c17d`, release: the program loads, the inner pattern matches nothing, so the
;;; `(absent …)` holds, and the read-out answers *the goal holds* beside `(says
;;; (paid Bob))`, exit 0 on every command.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.1 (T1f.7.1.3).

(relation says Guest :why "{?1} says something")
(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(says (paid Bob))
(solve :hypothesis-relations ())
(query :goal (absent (says (?R ?g))))
